 money  i mean that is an open question  as to how that capital will be deployed  in the future  one thing that could happen is  these funds could start doing deals that  involve some debt elements or  you know more investor protections for  equity that they buy  you see that a lot in down cycles and  and that could be a way in which some of  the capital is invested  so the time of easy money seems to be  over for startups i guess right sadly  for the startups and i guess maybe the  investors as well  all right that's our reporter berber gin  thanks so much for joining us berber  thanks so i appreciate it  and that's it for today's tech news  briefing if you want more tech stories  check out our website wsj.com  and if you like our show please rate and  review it you can do that wherever you  get your podcasts  i'm zoe thomas for the wall street  journal  thanks for listening  [Music]  you

